# The read walk `for(&xs, …)` (B7a) lets its body READ the walked collection.
# Before the value flip (B8) the body could share its handle (`h := xs`) and
# grow it through the share, and the loop's guard (`xs`'s runtime borrow flag)
# made that push panic instead of reallocating the buffer under the live
# element reference `x`. A value list has no shared handle: `h := xs` moves
# the walked list, which the loop's `&` borrow rejects at compile time (E0911).
# Since R-FOR the loop is the value form over `(&xs).into_iter()`: the cursor's
# items hold the `&xs` lend, so the move is rejected whichever binding the
# message names.
stdout_keep_match=error\[E0911\]: Cannot move .xs. here: .[a-z_0-9]+. borrows .xs. with .&. and is still live.*|--> src/main\.yo:[0-9]+:[0-9]+
timeout=300
